# Go packing checklist for {{KTM_CREATE_PROJECT_NAME}}

Use this checklist before changing `ktm-pack.json`, `scripts/build.sh`, or package modes for this Go SDK project.

## Mode checklist

### `compiled`

- [ ] `scripts/build.sh` writes built binaries to `$KTM_BUILD_OUTPUT/compiled/bin`.
- [ ] The `compiled` list includes `compiled` only.
- [ ] The archive contains `compiled/bin/{{KTM_CREATE_PROJECT_NAME}}`.
- [ ] The archive does not contain Go source roots such as `source/`, `cmd/`, `internal/`, or `examples/`.
- [ ] The archive does not contain `docs/` by default.

Run:

```bash
ktm pack --platform {{KTM_CREATE_PRIMARY_PLATFORM}} --mode compiled
```

### `compiled-source`

- [ ] `scripts/build.sh` writes the canonical source snapshot to `$KTM_BUILD_OUTPUT/source`.
- [ ] The `source` list includes `source`. If a composed mode repeats a path, KTM deduplicates it before packaging.
- [ ] The archive contains both `compiled/` and `source/` roots.
- [ ] Source snapshots exclude generated build/test caches.

Run:

```bash
ktm pack --platform {{KTM_CREATE_PRIMARY_PLATFORM}} --mode compiled-source
```
## Shared package safety checklist

- [ ] Confirm the requested mode is `compiled` or `compiled-source`.
- [ ] Edit `ktm-pack.json` lists instead of hardcoding paths in KTM.
- [ ] Keep lists composable and reviewable. Repeated paths are allowed, but KTM deduplicates them before packaging.
- [ ] Keep `docs/` out of package payload unless Daniel explicitly asks to package docs.
- [ ] Keep generated caches out of payload.
- [ ] Ensure `scripts/build.sh` writes intentional payload roots to `$KTM_BUILD_OUTPUT`.
- [ ] Validate with `ktm doctor`, `ktm dev`, `ktm test`, and both pack modes when changing packaging behavior.
- [ ] Inspect the resulting archive when payload composition changes.
- [ ] Verify kt-node stays KTM-managed in normal compiled modes; do not vendor dependency libraries into the package.

## Dependency ownership / eject review

The default pack modes keep `kinematic-trees/libkt@{{KTM_CREATE_KT_NODE_VERSION}}` as a KTM-managed dependency. A normal compiled or compiled-source package must not copy KTM store paths, dependency shared libraries, headers, or metadata into the project payload.

A future eject/self-contained flow should be explicit and separately reviewed because it changes who owns dependency updates, license notices, SBOM evidence, and security patching. Until that flow exists, `ktm pack --mode eject` is expected to fail rather than silently vendor dependencies.

## Quick payload inspection

After packing, inspect contents with:

```bash
tar -tzf _pack/*/{{KTM_CREATE_PRIMARY_PLATFORM}}/*.tar.gz | sort
```

Expected defaults:

- `compiled`: only runtime/compiled payload roots.
- `compiled-source`: runtime/compiled payload roots plus separate source-list roots.
- `docs/`: present in the generated project folder, absent from archives by default.
- `deps/`, `.ktrees/`, KTM store paths, and kt-node dependency libraries: absent from normal pack archives.
